 ## Overview
-Expected Term Rendering computes the expected termination distance (depth) for each ray traversing a volume, returning a tensor of size $Q$ (number of rays) [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from standard depth rendering by calculating the weighted mean of sample depths along the ray, where weights are derived from the volume's transmittance and absorption properties [G]. This method builds on [Depth from Ray Distance](5665-depth-from-ray-distance.md) by specifically implementing the expected value strategy for depth estimation [S2, unofficial].
